{"id": "q0414", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's been a while since I've written anything down. The days blend together now, each one feeling the same as the last—s ilent, empty, and heavy with loneliness. I keep thinking about how things used to be. The noise of cars outside my window, the laughter of children playing in the park, even the smell of fresh bread from the bake ry down the street—all gone now.I remember standing at the edge of town one morning, watching people gather for what they thought would be their last meal. No one knew it was the beginning of the end. Now, there' s just me. I wander the streets like a ghost, checking empty stores, turning on lights that flicker but never stay lit. Sometimes I talk to myself, not really expecting an answer, but hoping maybe someone will hear me. The silence is so thick it feels alive, pressing in around me. I wonder if anyone else out there feels this way— lost, alone, searching for meaning in nothingness. But then I remember: I am the only one left. The weight of that truth settles over me again, cold and real. I try to find comfort in small things—the sun on my face, the", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
